.TH "DATATRANSFERITEM.TYPE" "3JS" "August 31, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DataTransferItem.type \- DataTransferItem: type property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]type\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]DataTransferItem\f[R] interface returns the type (format) of the
object representing the drag data item.
The \f[CR]type\f[R] is a Unicode string generally given by a MIME type,
although a MIME type is not required.
.PP
Some example types are: \f[CR]text/plain\f[R] and \f[CR]text/html\f[R].
.PP
During a drag operation, this property can be read in any drag event
handler, even when the drag data store is in protected mode.
The item\(cqs type remains accessible, but its data can only be read in
the handlers for the \f[CR]dragstart\f[R] and \f[CR]drop\f[R] events.
See Reading the drag data store for details.
.SH VALUE
A string representing the drag data item\(cqs type.
.SH EXAMPLES
This example shows the use of the \f[CR]type\f[R] property.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] dropHandler(ev) {
  console.log(\(dqDrop\(dq);
  ev.preventDefault();
  \f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] item \f[B]of\f[R] ev.dataTransfer.items) {
    \f[B]if\f[R] (item.kind === \(dqstring\(dq && item.type.match(\(dq\(hatext/plain\(dq)) {
      \f[I]// This item is the target node\f[R]
      item.getAsString((s) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
        ev.target.appendChild(document.getElementById(s));
      });
    } \f[B]else\f[R] \f[B]if\f[R] (item.kind === \(dqstring\(dq && item.type.match(\(dq\(hatext/html\(dq)) {
      \f[I]// Drag data item is HTML\f[R]
      console.log(\(dq\&... Drop: HTML\(dq);
    } \f[B]else\f[R] \f[B]if\f[R] (item.kind === \(dqstring\(dq && item.type.match(\(dq\(hatext/uri\-list\(dq)) {
      \f[I]// Drag data item is URI\f[R]
      console.log(\(dq\&... Drop: URI\(dq);
    } \f[B]else\f[R] \f[B]if\f[R] (item.kind === \(dqfile\(dq && item.type.match(\(dq\(haimage/\(dq)) {
      \f[I]// Drag data item is an image file\f[R]
      \f[B]const\f[R] f = item.getAsFile();
      console.log(\(dq\&... Drop: File\(dq);
    }
  }
}
.EE
